From 381f1196a0618b6c49111bd6f77e2d1279268282 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:46:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-3mg3-cr28-46gc (CVE-2026-129292): escape client data
 in FPM status page

The full FPM status page printed the request method, request URI, auth
user and script filename raw. In 7.2 the query string was escaped only
for html/xml and with flags ENT_HTML_IGNORE_ERRORS & ENT_COMPAT (= 0, so
quotes were not escaped), and the JSON output was never escaped, so the
older GHSA-7qg2-v9fj-4mwv (CVE-2026-6735) request URI fix is missing in
7.2 as well. This closes both.

Backport of php-src 37abd0a7f7 (which builds on 99a5ad7441) to 7.2.34:
- A common fpm_status_escape() helper is used for request method,
  request URI, query string, auth user and script filename.
- html and xml: php_escape_html_entities_ex() with the 7.2 signature
  (no quiet argument) and ENT_QUOTES | ENT_HTML_IGNORE_ERRORS |
  ENT_DISALLOWED | ENT_HTML_DOC_XML1 (upstream uses ENT_COMPAT; single
  quotes are escaped too here).
- json: 7.2 FPM cannot rely on ext/json (it may be disabled or shared
  in 7.2), so a small static escaper is used instead of
  php_json_encode_string(): '"' and '\' are backslash-escaped, control
  characters below 0x20 become \u00XX.
- text/plain output is unchanged.
- The test is rewritten for the 7.2 FPM tester (no multiRequest()): a
  raw async FastCGI request keeps one worker busy while the status page
  is fetched in html, xml and json format.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
