From 2cdcc2b05c0724850667364621e4afebea18b3ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:09:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-q6x7-frmf-grcw (CVE-2024-3096): password_hash() with
 a leading NUL byte

bcrypt stops at the first NUL byte, so a password starting with "\0"
hashed like the empty password, and password_verify() then accepted an
empty password for that hash. password_hash() with bcrypt now fails with
a warning ("Bcrypt password must not contain null character"), so no
such hash is created.

Backport of php-src 0ba5229a3f (Jakub Zelenka), same change as Sury's 7.2
patch 0120.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
