From 1120331cb548dd84c098d072db2c59001094738e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:09:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-9pqp-7h25-4f32 (CVE-2024-8925): multipart boundary
 longer than the read buffer

A multipart/form-data boundary longer than the parser's read buffer was
parsed wrongly, so form fields and uploads could be split or merged in
ways the sender did not intend. Boundaries are now limited to what the
parser handles correctly (FILLUNIT - 4 bytes, more than the 70 that
RFC 1521 allows). With a longer one the body is not parsed and a
"Boundary too large" warning is logged.

Backport of php-src 19b49258d0 (Arnaud Le Blanc) with its follow-ups
c70e256308 (skip the test on Windows) and Remi Collet's 7.x test
adaptation; same change as Sury's 7.2 patches 0126, 0129 and 0131.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 main/rfc1867.c                       |   7 ++
 tests/basic/GHSA-9pqp-7h25-4f32.inc  |   3 +
 tests/basic/GHSA-9pqp-7h25-4f32.phpt | 104 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 114 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/basic/GHSA-9pqp-7h25-4f32.inc
 create mode 100644 tests/basic/GHSA-9pqp-7h25-4f32.phpt

diff --git a/main/rfc1867.c b/main/rfc1867.c
index f6cbc763..6659fc45 100644
--- a/main/rfc1867.c
+++ b/main/rfc1867.c
@@ -783,6 +783,13 @@ SAPI_API SAPI_POST_HANDLER_FUNC(rfc1867_post_handler) /* {{{ */
 		boundary_len = boundary_end-boundary;
 	}
 
+	/* Boundaries larger than FILLUNIT-strlen("\r\n--") characters lead to
+	 * erroneous parsing */
+	if (boundary_len > FILLUNIT-strlen("\r\n--")) {
+		sapi_module.sapi_error(E_WARNING, "Boundary too large in multipart/form-data POST data");
+		return;
+	}
+
 	/* Initialize the buffer */
 	if (!(mbuff = multipart_buffer_new(boundary, boundary_len))) {
 		sapi_module.sapi_error(E_WARNING, "Unable to initialize the input buffer");
