From b40635f1aff4d3a8b0c204901362576975e79ffc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:09:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-cj93-vc83-wgqv (CVE-2025-14181): SoapClient chunked
 response length overflow

SoapClient kept the size of a chunked response in an int, so a server
sending 2 GB or more overflowed it and the client wrote past its buffer.
Sizes are now size_t with overflow checks and safe (re)allocation; the
redirect Location path allocation is overflow-checked too.

Backport of php-src b11bd1d939 (Nora Dossche, Jakub Zelenka) with the
test rework 3aedde06bc (Jakub Zelenka) and Sury's two test fixes for
7.2 (SKIPIF; this version does not trim the Transfer-Encoding value);
same change as Sury's 7.2 patches 0196, 0197, 0198 and 0216. The fix
frees a buffer with zend_string_efree(), which PHP 7.2 does not have
yet (7.3+), so Sury's 0171 adds that inline helper to Zend/zend_string.h
here as well.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
