Subject: [PATCH] ext/soap: SAFE_STR casts to const char * (follow-up to
 CVE-2021-21702)

The CVE-2021-21702 backport added SAFE_STR(a) ((a)?a:""). With an
xmlChar * argument the two branches have different pointer types, which
newer gcc rejects (an error without -fpermissive). The upstream build fix
casts the pointer.

Backport of php-src e5d767d27f (Nikita Popov), same change as Sury's 7.2
patch 0060; part of fajxo/issue-tracking#205 batch A+B.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
