From c017e3331bad78dded14ab10852ad9c1b8cf0fed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:39:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix #78719: http wrapper ignores long response header lines

Response header lines longer than HTTP_HEADER_BLOCK_SIZE (1024 bytes)
were dropped without a word, so a long Location was not followed and
other long headers vanished. Header lines of any length are now read.
The GHSA-v8xr and GHSA-52jp fixes below are written on top of this
code; 52jp then limits a Location to 8182 bytes.

Backport of php-src 51e2015af3 (Christoph M. Becker), Sury's 7.2 patch
0172. 7.4.33 has it; 7.2 was security-only by then.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
