From 47bc939ae12a74f310ec9b759406ee8d2b56a20a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:39:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-v8xr-gpvj-cx9g (CVE-2025-1217): http response header
 folding

The http wrapper treated a folded (continuation) response header line
as a new header, so a server could smuggle a Location or Content-Type
past the parser. Folded lines are now joined onto the header they
continue, as RFC 7230 describes. http_response_header_05.phpt tested
the old behaviour and is removed upstream.

Backport of php-src d20b4c97a9 (Jakub Zelenka), Sury's 7.2 patch 0176.
The new tests use their own copy of the 7.4 ServerClientTestCase.inc
(ephemeral ports) in ext/standard/tests/http, Sury's 0177, so the
fixed-port helper in ext/openssl/tests that the older tests use stays
as it is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
