From e601ccf467905c3809436c2a9b7189e1fda5cc90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:39:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-pcmh-g36c-qc44 (CVE-2025-1734): http headers without
 a colon

A response header line without a colon was accepted, which lets a
malformed or hostile response be read differently by PHP and by
proxies in between. Such a line now makes the request fail; bug47021
and bug75535 tests change accordingly.

Backport of php-src 0548c4c175 (Jakub Zelenka), Sury's 7.2 patch 0178.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
