From 2c62bc4c384f5dbfed410283c99660d7db84de1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:39:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix out-of-bounds read on an empty Location header (GH-23467)

An empty Location allocates one byte, and the relative-redirect branch
read location[1] past it, so a server could make the client follow a
redirect built from heap garbage. The branch now uses the stored length
and skips the join for an empty Location. The follow-up GH-23521
restores the old handling of a one-character Location (resolved
against the host root, as before).

Backport of php-src 547566f17a (Ilia Alshanetsky) and 64664758cd
(Jordi Kroon), Sury's 7.2 patches 0180 and 0181.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
