From 9b52557cd39aaa89e78137f073116affac8b3eb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:39:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-vvx9-73fr-5jjx (CVE-2026-91769): no CN fallback
 after SAN

Peer name verification fell back to the subject CN when no DNS SAN
matched, even if the certificate carried DNS, SRV or URI SANs. RFC 6125
6.4.4 forbids that: a CA that validated only the SAN identities could
leave an unvalidated CN that PHP then accepted as a host name. IP-only
SAN certificates keep the CN fallback.

Backport of php-src 0bb308eb4c (Jakub Zelenka), Sury's 7.2 patch 0204.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
