From de3cf8081aa58421c7e4a87ed96f214109ced1a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:34:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bug #81211: symlinks followed when creating a phar

Phar::buildFromDirectory() and buildFromIterator() checked only that
the base directory string occurred somewhere in the file name, so a
symlink pointing outside the base (or a sibling directory sharing its
prefix) was added to the archive. The name must start with the base
and continue with a path separator.

Backport of php-src 2ff853aa11 (Christoph M. Becker), Sury's 7.2 patch
0075. 7.4 has it since 7.4.21.

The test expects %e as the directory separator, as upstream's copy in
7.4.33 does; Sury's copy has Windows backslashes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
