From c270327fc346ba1ceb6fef857e1c40bab9bc0ebb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:34:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bug #79971 (CVE-2021-21707): NUL in URIs given to libxml
 functions

The libxml based functions that take a file name (simplexml_load_file(),
DOMDocument::load(), XMLReader::open(), xmlwriter_open_uri(), ...)
accept URIs, and a percent-encoded NUL (%00) truncated the path the
same way a raw NUL would. Reject such URIs with a warning.

Backport of php-src f15f8fc573 (Christoph M. Becker), Sury's 7.2 patch
0083. 7.4 has it since 7.4.26.

bug79971_1.phpt accepts the libxml2 >= 2.13 wording (failed to load
"file:///...": No such file or directory) as well as the old one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
