Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:34:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bug #81738 (CVE-2022-37454): SHA-3 overflow on inputs
 over 4 GB

The bundled Keccak sponge cast the remaining input length to a 32-bit
unsigned int before its bound check, so hash_update() with sha3-* and
an input of 4 GB or more passed the check and wrote past the state
buffer. Check the 64-bit length first. memory_limit makes this hard to
reach on our pools; fixed because the code is ours to carry.

Backport of php-src de4517ad60 (Stanislav Malyshev), Sury's 7.2 patch
0096. 7.4 has it since 7.4.33.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
