From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:34:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ext/openssl: openssl_encrypt() heap overflow with
 AES-WRAP-PAD

openssl_encrypt() sized the output for the input plus one cipher
block. In wrap mode (AES-WRAP-PAD, RFC 5649) the input is rounded up
to the block size and an integrity block is prepended, so the cipher
could write past the zend_mm allocation. Reserve one more block in
wrap mode.

Backport of php-src GH-22187 (David Carlier), Sury's 7.2 patch 0153.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ext/openssl/openssl.c          | 15 ++++++++++++++-
