From 520de5ffacfc742d3be8d2d2ecffc0d5b99ba9b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:34:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-h35g-vwh6-m678 (CVE-2024-8929): mysqlnd heap
 over-reads

A hostile or spoofed MySQL server could make mysqlnd read past its
packet buffers (COM_LIST field defaults, upsert filename, OK message,
binary row fields of every type) and return heap content to the script.
Also bounds the auth_protocol name in the greeting packet.

Backport of php-src (Jakub Zelenka) as Sury's 7.2 patches 0166 (fix),
0167 (auth_protocol over-read), 0168-0170 (fake server tests, Remi
Collet's adaptation), 0212 (binary row bound for 7.2: the chunk size
includes the preallocated bytes, use the data size) and 0213 (tests
for 7.2's client packets).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
