From 13bb2493e62023008e69642eb1ce847f3254a2e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:34:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-www2-q4fc-65wf: NUL bytes in dns_get_record() and
 friends

inet_pton(), ip2long(), getservbyname(), getservbyport(),
getprotobyname() and the host name functions in dns.c
(dns_check_record(), dns_get_record(), dns_get_mx() and others) took
their name as a C string, so a name with a NUL byte was silently
truncated. They now parse it as a path argument, which rejects NUL.

Backport of php-src ed70b1ea43 (Niels Dossche), Sury's 7.2 patch 0190.

The wrong-type warnings of these functions now say "expects parameter N
to be a valid path" instead of "to be string", as upstream since the
change; getservbyname_variation1/6/8/13 and ip2long_variation1 are
updated for that.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
