From 3a1cba2e560029ece615c4fce85b636abab566cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:34:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-j3wh-g957-2m85 (CVE-2026-6103): phar tar entry
 injection

phar_tar_number() accepted sizes it could not represent, and entries
of some types were not skipped by their data size, so the reader could
be left inside attacker data and parse it as the next tar header.
Reject such sizes and skip the data blocks of every entry type that
carries data.

Backport of php-src 0994e2e887 (Jakub Zelenka), Sury's 7.2 patch 0208.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
